# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
opnsense2otel-security-findings/
# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
*opnsense2otel-local
local.Makefile
key
secret
local.docker-compose.yml
.DS_Store

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
# .env.example is generated by `make docs` and is a reference, not a credential
# store: every line is commented out. Without this negation the generator writes a
# file git never sees, and `make docs-check` fails in CI on a fresh clone.
!.env.example

# IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/

/opnsense2otel
# Kept alongside the current name: a checkout that predates the opnsense2otel
# rename leaves a binary called opnsense-exporter at the root, and renaming this
# entry alone would silently un-ignore it into the next `git add -A`.
/opnsense-exporter
/docgen
# Stray dev binaries from `go build ./cmd/...`
/apicapture
/apicontract

# Release-artifact tooling + outputs (regenerated at release time; never committed):
# pinned tool binaries, built binary, SBOMs, third-party notices.
/.tools/
/bin/
/dist/
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

# Python (grafana dashboard/rules builders)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# zensical local build output. The published site is built independently by the
# rknightion/m7kni-net-site hub from docs/ + zensical.toml; nothing in this repo
# consumes a committed build tree, so keep it untracked.
/site/

# Superpowers scratch (specs/plans) + local roadmap — never committed
docs/superpowers/
/roadmap.md

# Response-shape canary captures (make capture) — scratch real-box payloads.
# Review one (it may contain host/network data) and promote it into a curated
# fixture (opnsense/testdata/health/...) to make it a permanent CI gate.
/opnsense/testdata/captures/

# Claude Code local session state (settings.local.json, agent scratch). Nothing here
# is shared configuration — the repo's committed guidance lives in CLAUDE.md.
/.claude/

# Injected by the m7kni.io hub at build time — never commit these.
# The hub copies its own SEO template, brand stylesheet and fonts into a clone
# and generates zensical.toml from docs.toml. A tracked copy here is drift, and
# is exactly what the manifest model exists to prevent.
/zensical.toml
docs/overrides/
docs/stylesheets/brand.css
docs/fonts/
